# `disconnect p0` while p0 owned the attachment a2 and was a page client of main. The Rust runner
# severed every connection of p0, including the one p1's writer held to p0 as a2's owner, so p1's
# commit failed 08006 there while Go and TypeScript, which end only p0's connection to main's owner,
# committed it (simulation-testing.md §5). Shrunk from service-attachments seed 37.
# format: simulation
# profile: service-attachments
# seed: 37
# page_size: 512
# cache_bytes: 2048
# processes: service
# clock: 1700000000000000
spawn p2
attach a2
spawn p1
kill p0
backup page_identical p2
spawn p0
open w9 write p1
disconnect p0
commit w9
